# Line endings are LF in every working tree, on every platform.
#
# Not a style preference — a correctness one. scripts/check-claims.mjs verifies
# quoted figures by re-measuring the files they describe, and CRLF adds a byte
# per line. A Windows checkout with the default core.autocrlf=true measured
# ARCHITECTURE.md at 1,867 tokens where Linux CI measured 1,834, so the same
# README was simultaneously accurate on CI and wrong on a developer's laptop.
# Pinning eol=lf makes those measurements mean the same thing everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats git must never touch.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.mp4 binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ico binary
